Pushing a new line to this file fires .github/workflows/news-scan.yml (the
German A1 lesson pipeline) through its `push` trigger, and NOTHING ELSE.

That exclusivity is the whole point. .trigger-daily-dispatch is listened to
by BOTH daily.yml and news-scan.yml, and all three production workflows share
the "gapmedia-production" concurrency group with cancel-in-progress: false.
GitHub keeps only ONE pending run per group, so when a single push creates two
runs in that group, the second one queued cancels the first — measured live
2026-09-13: runs #223/#228 (news-scan survived, daily cancelled) and #229/#230
(daily survived, news-scan cancelled) came from identical pushes. Which one
lives is a coin flip.

lib/recovery-chain.mjs pushes THIS file instead, so a chained Recovery Loop
retry can never be cancelled by daily.yml before it runs.

